// `--no-bounds` gives back the unchecked read, and says nothing about it.
//
// This is the same read `bounds_read` makes, run with the flag. What it asserts
// is not only that the program finishes, but that the build is silent: `--no-bounds`
// used to be collected as an unrecognized argument and handed to the link step,
// where the C compiler warns that the option is valid for Modula-2 and not for C.
// The read worked anyway, so the flag looked like it did its job while every
// build that used it printed a warning from a tool the caller never named.
//
// A program in that state is a program whose warnings nobody can act on, so the
// harness compares the combined output byte for byte rather than looking for the
// value alone.

var a = new int[2];
a[0] = 7;
a[1] = 9;
Console.WriteLog(a[5]);
